\description{
This module function allows to apply a diverse set of Feature attribtion methods on a fitted \code{abcnn} neural network
and a given observed dataset, in order to compute the weight of each summary statistic on predictions.
Summary statistics with the higher weight (or importance) are those contributing the most to the prediction.

This feature importance method is useful to perform feature selection (removing summary statistics that don't explain well the output)
and to interpret properly the output of the model.
}
\details{
All the methods used in explain are implemented in the \code{innsight} R package, that is part of the R torch ecosystem. These methods are:
\itemize{
\item Vanilla Gradient and GradientxInput
\item SmoothGrand and SmoothGradxInput
\item Integrated Gradients
\item Expected Gradients
\item Layer-Wise Relevance Propagation (LRP)
\item Deep learning important features (DeepLift)
\item Deep Shapley additive explanations (DeepSHAP)
\item Connection weights method
\item Local interpretable model-agnostic explanations (LIME)
\item Shapley values (SHAP)
}

See \verb{https://bips-hb.github.io/innsight/} for details.
}
